# Line-ending policy.
#
# Phaser compares committed golden output byte for byte, and reproduces fuzz
# findings from committed corpus inputs byte for byte. Neither survives a
# version-control system that rewrites line endings per platform, so this file
# takes that decision away from the checkout.

# Every text file is LF in the working tree on every platform, including
# Windows, where Git would otherwise check out CRLF and make each golden
# comparison fail on an invisible difference.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fuzz corpora are byte-exact regression inputs: the bytes are the test. They
# are marked binary explicitly rather than left to Git's content heuristic,
# which classifies a file as text when it finds no NUL byte -- and most of these
# inputs have none while still containing 0x0A bytes that a conversion would
# rewrite. A corrupted corpus entry does not fail loudly; it silently stops
# reproducing the finding it was minimized from.
test/corpus/** -text
